<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids lower, trade slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids lower, trade slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids were mostly lower Thursday in line with a drop in spring wheat futures at the Minneapolis Grain Exchange, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>Movement of wheat remained slow, although one Montana dealer noted a brief flurry of selling early.</p>
<p>&quot;We had a couple of guys bail out of a few thousand bushels before the market started going down, but then we had nothing for the rest of the day,&quot; the Montana dealer said.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat fell after USDA's winter wheat output estimate came in above the average of analysts' expectations.</p>
